WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.225
For many agencies, neither SD-WAN
nor a new TIC use case is close.

2
00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:08.863
The acquisition isn't funded and
the task orders aren't placed.

3
00:00:08.863 --> 00:00:11.791
The book calls that
interval the long interim,

4
00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:16.338
and argues the architecture by
elimination, because no mandate exists.

5
00:00:16.338 --> 00:00:20.276
The hairpin is still permitted,
but CISA's own guidebook says it

6
00:00:20.276 --> 00:00:24.437
raised the cost and cut the
effectiveness of TIC for cloud services.

7
00:00:24.437 --> 00:00:28.925
A new agency-run access point is
a capital and staffing commitment.

8
00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:32.125
VPN backhaul is a hairpin
under another name.

9
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:36.433
What's left is local breakout, a
cloud-delivered security stack nearby,

10
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:38.662
and a policy layer at the branch edge.

11
00:00:38.662 --> 00:00:43.789
The target is years away for structural
reasons: acquisition takes quarters,

12
00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:46.592
budget submissions go to OMB in September,

13
00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:51.238
and a thousand branches is a multi-year
deployment on logistics alone.

14
00:00:51.238 --> 00:00:52.887
But the interval isn't empty.

15
00:00:52.887 --> 00:00:57.438
Four of the six branch-edge functions
are partly obtainable before any award.

16
00:00:57.438 --> 00:01:00.388
The decision belongs to
the authorizing official.

17
00:01:00.388 --> 00:01:05.099
Record which control assertions depend on
transport evidence that doesn't exist,

18
00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:08.425
the compensating measures, and
the funded plan to fix them.

19
00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:12.300
An undocumented gap found by
an assessor is a finding.

20
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.713
A documented gap with a
plan is an accepted risk.

21
00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:16.600
Do it now.

22
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.180
Next, the most important planning item.
